hair is made of long strands of a  protein called keratin some people have  hair follicles that produce keratin that  different rates across the hair these  people have curly hair to curl here the  keratin strands on the outside of each  hair are stretched and dried the bonds  reform with one side longer than the  other and you get curls high humidity  allows hair to reabsorb water and  straighten out again the shape that  curly hairs make is a helix a coil the  same as that found in the structure of  DNA there are equations which can  describe how the helix will look where x  y&amp;z denote what's happening in each  direction R is the radius of the curl L  is the length of the curl and sine and  cos are relations from trigonometry if  we just look at the x-direction  it's a cosine wave like this and in the  y-direction we have a sine wave like  this these waves can be used to model  many different types of oscillating  cycles that occur throughout nature such  as sound waves visible light waves and  radio waves when we put it together with  another dimension zid letting the waves  move forward over a distance we get this  one complete curl is one cycle of the  wave the distance required to complete  one full cycle varies for every one if a  person's hair completes one full curl  cycle every ten centimeters then in 30  centimeters of hair there will be three  full curls but if they cut it short -  less than ten centimeters it would  appear straight or slightly wavy on the  other hand if someone had very curly  hair  a cycle every one centimeter then  cutting it short would not make it look  straight and it would be even bouncier  from the lack of weight
 

